  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Website Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the design elements of the Reidius Infra website. I\'m taking notes on color palettes, typography, image usage, and overall layout. The goal is to identify best practices that can be applied to the Sanchar Infratech website to achieve a more modern and professional look. I\'ll compare it to the second referenced website shortly.\n\n\n**Evaluating Website Features**\n\nI\'ve been mentally cataloging key features for the new site. I\'m imagining a hero section, live stats, and scrolling branding. I\'m also thinking of a services marquee, categorized projects with filtering, and a \"Transparency\" section with a mock live camera view. A cost estimator, a Vastu guide popup, officials section, and contact form are on my list, too.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on specific design components of Reidiusinfra. The \"Expertise\" layout, with its numerical emphasis and staggered visuals, is a key point of inspiration. Parallax backgrounds and detailed footers are also notable. I\'m considering refining interactions for project cards with slide-up effects and data reveals, possibly even adding a custom cursor, and implementing micro-interactions, like staggered list animations.\n\n\n**Incorporating Visual Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating design elements from Reidiusinfra. I\'m focusing on their grid, and the use of quality badges is something I want to incorporate. I\'m adding a parallax hero element and considering a Quality & Certifications section. The projects section will be \"Pinterest-style\", and I\'m updating the navbar with a glassmorphism effect. I\'m also planning a \"Why Choose Us\" section. I\'ll be updating animations and enhancing the Services Marquee. My next step is examining `src/App.tsx` for integration points. Specifically, I\'m going to refine the hero, with a parallax effect, and enhance the stats section.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now refine the Sanchar Infratech website to more closely mirror the high-end, architectural aesthetic and functional depth of the reference sites. This includes adding a parallax hero effect, enhancing the bento-style layouts for core values, and implementing a more sophisticated project gallery that feels like a professional portfolio.\n\n1.  **Hero Parallax**: Add a smooth parallax effect to the hero image for a more immersive entry.\n2.  **Bento Layout for Expertise**: Reconstruct the \"Why Choose Us\" section into a modern bento grid.\n3.  **Refined Typography & Spacing**: Adjust scales to ensure a premium \"editorial\" feel.\n4.  **Interactive Portfolio**: Enhance project cards with more detailed hover states.\n5.  **Corporate Credibility**: Add a specific section for \"Quality & Standards\" to reinforce the infratech branding.\n\nLet\'s start by reading the design guidelines to ensure I follow best practices for this aesthetic.\n\n### Skill Check:\n1. [RELEVANT] frontend-design: Essential for the \"minimalist and aesthetic\" request.\n2. [RELEVANT] image-generation: (Though previously exhausted, I will use high-quality Unsplash URLs as fallback).\n\nI\'ll read `SKILL.md` for `frontend-design`.\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 529025088
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
