th `Wind`. The hierarchy review was useful, especially clarifying the rotating dot element. I\'m focusing on that third div and the associated code block now.\n\n\n**Clarifying Icon Target**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the target of the proposed icon change, as it seems I was initially mistaken. I\'m reevaluating whether the rotating dot or the encompassing `Compass` itself is what the user wants to modify. I am reviewing the structure now: the rotating dot container is `div:nth-of-type(3)`, and the `Compass` is `div:nth-of-type(4)`, or is it the whole thing? I am doing a code review to confirm.\n\n\n**Verifying Icon Section**\n\nI\'ve made a key discovery. I was off by two sections in my selection of `nth-of-type`. The correct element is actually `TransparencySection` and not `VastuSection`. The section is the 10th `section` child, not the 12th as I previously thought. I\'ll need to update my code to reflect this corrected selection, which changes the target section for the icon revamp.\n\n\n**Confirming Icon Target**\n\nOkay, after some digging, I\'ve confirmed the target section is indeed `section#consultancy`, which I had correctly identified earlier as the Vastu section. However, I got confused with the `nth-of-type` selector, the correct one is the 10th child `section`. It\'s the `Compass` I need to replace, not the dot. I\'m leaning toward a more appealing replacement like `Stars`, `Sparkles` or `DraftingCompass`. Now, I\'ll start testing `DraftingCompass` and others, to meet the goal of enhancing appeal.\n\n\n**Deciding Icon Choice**\n\nI\'m now deciding between icon options, considering the user\'s feedback. I\'m focusing on `Sun` for the cosmic alignment concept, and I\'ll test `Wind` with a minimal design. I\'m focusing on replacing the existing `Compass` icon, not the rotating dot, although I might add some flair. I\'m also now analyzing the code for the compass icon implementation, and I am thinking about how to integrate a `Wind` icon there. I\'ll focus on 