  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Mixed Content**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"many sections are blank\" issue. The primary culprit appears to be mixed content, specifically the `BRANDS` array. I\'ve confirmed that the image `http://www.jaipurclub.in/images/logo.png` is blocked due to HTTPS restrictions, directly impacting visibility.\n\n\n**Refining the Logo Solution**\n\nI\'m now implementing the logo fix. My focus has shifted to ensuring a robust visual presence. The plan is a custom logo component with an `hasError` state. If the initial logo fails or future attempts error, it\'ll trigger a beautiful, themed initials-based icon fallback. This ensures consistent branding even with URL issues. I\'m also exploring reliable public image URLs and inline SVG alternatives, in conjunction with the custom component. Finally, I\'ll incorporate working brand logo URLs as needed.\n\n\n**Investigating Image Loading**\n\nI\'m now investigating image loading issues across multiple potential sources. I\'m cross-referencing user updates, particularly the WordPress uploads from `sancharinfratech.com`, to confirm if any are blank. I\'m verifying the URLs provided by the user, and re-checking whether the issue extends beyond the logo to other image-dependent sections, such as the `OFFICIALS` section where I\'ve identified `Akhilesh Mittal`\'s image URL to check.\n\n\n**Examining Team Image Sources**\n\nI\'m now diving into the team images. I\'ve noted three URLs from Unsplash for Pushpendra Kumar Mittal, Manohar Kant, and Tanmaya Mittal, respectively. I\'m checking their loading behavior. Moreover, I\'m examining other sections, and double-checking that team images render correctly. This investigation aims to identify and rule out potential general image loading problems. I\'m focusing on the `BrandsTicker` section next, and evaluating its implementation.\n\n\n**Designing the Fallback Display**\n\nI\'ve got it! The blank `BrandsTicker` section is due to `display: \'none\'` on failing images. Now, the plan is to replace invisible images with a visually engaging fallback. I\'m exploring a stylish, high-contrast, initials-based icon or text-based replacement. The goal is to avoid blank spaces and maintain a cohesive design. I\'m leaning toward a card-like element with initials, ensuring a modern look.\n\n\n**Implementing the Fallback Text**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the text-based logo implementation. I\'m exploring using a React hook within a `BrandLogo` sub-component to track image loading state for each brand. The plan is to render a styled text-based fallback (e.g., \"JC\" for \"Jai Club\") with a clean visual style and a high-contrast theme, in the `BrandsTicker` section. The overall design focus is elegance and readability. The fallback design will have subtle borders, shadows and the `#9fc5e9` accent color. I\'ve re-confirmed the `BRANDS` array structure for data integrity.\n\n\n**Refining the Initial Code**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `BrandLogo` component. I\'m utilizing `hasError` to handle image loading. The plan is to gracefully display an elegant initials fallback. I am focusing on high-end minimalism and clean, concise code. I\'ve built the fallback with conditional rendering in React. It\'s now ready for testing, and I\'ll explore optimization techniques later.\n\n\n**Styling the Monogram**\n\nI\'m now implementing the polished monogram. When the `hasError` flag is triggered, I display a sophisticated container. This component has a border, a background, and the brand initials, designed to mimic a high-end corporate seal. I\'m focusing on a minimalist aesthetic to maintain a premium look and feel. The refined style uses a teal accent color, subtle shadows and rounded corners, creating a modern badge effect.\n\n\n**Verifying the Image Render**\n\nI\'m now running comprehensive tests. The monogram display is stunning, ensuring a professional fallback for all logos. I\'m verifying the successful rendering of the stylized emblem across all brand entries within the `BrandsTicker` section. I\'ve confirmed a smooth and consistent visual experience, eliminating blank spaces and gaps. Next, I\'ll be re-checking other sections, to verify if all images render successfully.\n\n\n**Expanding the Safety Net**\n\nI\'m now expanding the fallback system to address potential Unsplash image failures. My focus is on creating a robust solution to handle various loading issues. I\'m exploring a `<SafeImage>` component. I\'m also examining general image styling. The goal is a uniform, elegant display, preventing any empty image spaces. I\'m reviewing `src/App.tsx` and focusing on the `Team` component and other sections, specifically lines 1195 to 1230.\n\n\n"
