    summary: "You can find a wide variety of photos related to Indian luxury residential building architecture, modern office buildings, cricket stadiums, and construction sites on platforms like Unsplash, Getty Images, Shutterstock, and Alamy.\n\n**For Indian Luxury Residential Building Architecture:**\nUnsplash offers numerous images under categories like \"Indian house\" and \"Indian villa\"[1][2]. These may include designs ranging from traditional to modern luxury homes. Other platforms like Shutterstock also feature \"ultra-modern luxury apartment building exteriors in Pune\" and high-rise residential towers in Mumbai[3][4]. Buildofy, an architectural design platform, showcases top luxury homes across India, detailing their features and design[5].\n\n**For Indian Modern Office Buildings:**\nSeveral platforms provide extensive collections of Indian modern office buildings. Unsplash features images of \"Indian office\" and \"office India,\" including tall buildings with many windows and modern office interiors[6][7][8]. Getty Images and Shutterstock also offer thousands of stock photos of Indian office buildings, including commercial complexes with glass facades and corporate towers in various Indian cities like Bangalore, Hyderabad, and Mumbai[9][10][11]. Notable examples of modern office architecture in India include the Oval Office Building in Hyderabad, Nesco Tower 4 in Mumbai, and Advant Navis Business Park in Noida[12]. The Cybertecture Egg in Mumbai and the Infosys office in Mysore are also recognized for their unique designs[13].\n\n**For Indian Cricket Stadiums:**\nUnsplash is a good resource for images of Indian cricket stadiums, featuring photos of stadiums filled with spectators and views of famous grounds like Arun Jaitley Stadium in Delhi and Wankhede Stadium in Mumbai[14][15][16][17][18]. Other major stock photo sites like Shutterstock, Alamy, and Getty Images host thousands of royalty-free images of Indian cricket grounds, including aerial views of Eden Gardens in Kolkata and the M. Chinnaswamy Stadium in Bengaluru, as well as the Dharamshala Cricket Stadium nestled in the Himalayas[19][20][21][22][23].\n\n**For Indian Construction Site Photos:**\nUnsplash provides free-to-use images related to \"Indian construction\" and \"building India,\" including aerial views of construction sites[24][25][26][27]. Getty Images, Shutterstock, and Alamy offer vast collections of Indian construction site photos, with tens of thousands of images depicting various construction activities, tower cranes, workers, and developing cityscapes in places like Navi Mumbai, Gurgaon, and New Delhi[28][29][30][31][32].\n\nSources:\n[1] [unsplash.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEl0MU0LB1DI95HMBOEJBDLHNSl1FGPu9fcDReDc0ZUPwRT9M8wTVAHJeYbBQ36uqiZg7DfS1bRV0RvrtqZXSnYRANqzXAfLMsUTXPMimxjGbsxj9DoL3lEC3iE1mYaEje0tzYgjw==)\n[2] [unsplash.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEbf_jbJLa61LD-8Alup6E9X3nCfeO6OMSrLfLkZA6qeZVsqHfzKmU6O66yZ8fMJyI22W_T1hjhnGri5a0AZ33501HA6nSIBA1wndKHt3Q3wDLz4ek6-KQE6hV5dJdO-KhI-lqKjg==)\n[3] [shutterstock.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEU6j-4bgOurVM4mWRI8FF0pw2F2QDNwCgTjhtoMnUj0q_X_fNiC1UNXEUa5xGsG_3Kfi5BLZXow1Ub3591c9b9haK1BUXcofFVCR1IM3LavLZBOPMUAWM1ea14S_m9AoySpUIwkaXkD8QS2Nurups9AyP7icr0nto=)\n[4] [shutterstock.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHcOzY_m4qXxcILHVgJbYKsmjYxCH9s9MnxMAYsUTdap8ZTVNEytEio0snFIfeo4rHgIGTtj8pG8vXGGnqwWFl3_NDwmJA2K-n8LHYrLcqQtOTyiuk4qSodlnw-ii3Vc0Fp7198ybuR7fB_xJ2AybqsNFxXWY6pe67S)\n[5] [buildofy.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFiZx8T_MOTbB1glcRTz_ymjs4w0xZ-PwpB7rB9VVIs_0TFdZ6apr5O8tF0GP1H-SRnLt_w6HjkGDGvAIfPcZ19gsimwzVT0-Mi7Gjq92FvhfoU2wG96Y-TKMHApPUVOG5SZY6Djqo9lUKNCqgz7GRLMmwiGWoLdHR-lNyeoFbEi00=)\n[6] [unsplash.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFWE-H